   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "The name Falkland was applied to the channel by John Strong, captain of an English expedition that landed on the islands in 1690."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "The first undisputed landing on the islands is attributed to English captain John Strong, who, en route to Peru and Chile’s littoral in 1690, explored the Falkland Sound and noted the islands’ water and game."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "The name Falkland Islands comes from Falkland Sound, the strait that separates the two main islands."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "Although Fuegians from Patagonia may have visited the Falkland Islands in prehistoric times, the islands were uninhabited when Europeans first explored them."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "The Falkland Islands are a self-governing British Overseas Territory."
